  "title": "Ziyarat of Lady Aminah bint Wahb (s.a.), Mother of the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.)",
  "data": "At the grave of Lady Aminah (s.a.), mother of the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.), recite:\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكِ اَيَّتُهَا الطَّاهِرَةُ الْمُطَهَّرَةُ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKI AYYATUHAT TAAHIRATUL MUTAHHARAH\nPeace be upon you, O pure and purified one.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكِ يَا مَنْ خَصَّهَا اللّٰهُ بِاَعْلَى الشَّرَفِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKI YAA MAN KHASSAHALLAAHU BI-A'LASH SHARAF\nPeace be upon you, O you whom Allah singled out for the highest honour.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكِ يَا مَنْ سَطَعَ مِنْ جَبِيْنِهَا نُوْرُ سَيِّدِ الْاَنْبِيَاۤءِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKI YAA MAN SATA'A MIN JABEENIHAA NOORU SAYYIDIL ANBIYAA'\nPeace be upon you, O you from whose brow shone the light of the master of the prophets,\nفَاَضَاۤءَتْ بِهِ الْاَرْضُ وَالسَّمَاۤءُ\nFA-ADAA'AT BIHIL ARDU WAS SAMAA'\nso that the earth and the heavens were lit by it.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكِ يَا مَنْ نَزَلَتْ لِاَجْلِهَا الْمَلَاۤئِكَةُ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKI YAA MAN NAZALAT LI-AJLIHAL MALAA'IKAH\nPeace be upon you, O you for whose sake the angels came down,\nوَضُرِبَتْ لَهَا حُجُبُ الْجَنَّةِ\nWA DURIBAT LAHAA HUJUBUL JANNAH\nand for whom the curtains of Paradise were hung.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكِ يَا مَنْ نَزَلَتْ لِخِدْمَتِهَا الْحُوْرُ الْعِيْنُ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKI YAA MAN NAZALAT LIKHIDMATIHAL HOORUL I'EEN\nPeace be upon you, O you whom the houris came down to serve,\nوَسَقَيْنَهَا مِنْ شَرَابِ الْجَنَّةِ\nWA SAQAYNAHAA MIN SHARAABIL JANNAH\nwho gave you to drink from the drink of Paradise\nوَبَشَّرْنَهَا بِوِلَادَةِ خَيْرِ الْاَنْبِيَاۤءِ\nWA BASHSHARNAHAA BIWILAADATI KHAYRIL ANBIYAA'\nand gave you the glad tidings of the birth of the best of the prophets.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكِ يَا اُمَّ رَسُوْلِ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKI YAA UMMA RASOOLILLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O mother of the Messenger of Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكِ يَا اُمَّ حَبِيْبِ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKI YAA UMMA HABEEBILLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O mother of the beloved of Allah.\nفَهَنِيْۤئًا لَكِ بِمَا اٰتَاكِ اللّٰهُ مِنْ فَضْلٍ\nFAHANEE'AN LAKI BIMAA AATAAKILLAAHU MIN FADL\nJoy be yours, then, for the grace that Allah has given you.\nوَالسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكِ وَعَلٰى رَسُوْلِ اللّٰهِ صَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ وَاٰلِهٖ\nWAS SALAAMU A'LAYKI WA A'LAA RASOOLILLAAHI SALLALLAAHU A'LAYHI WA AALIH\nAnd peace be upon you and upon the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and his family,\nوَرَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهٗ\nWA RAHMATULLAAHI WA BARAKAATUH\nand the mercy of Allah and His blessings.",
  "merits": "Lady Aminah, daughter of Wahb ibn Abd Manaf of the Banu Zuhrah, was the mother of the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.). When the Prophet (s.a.w.a.) was six, she took him to Yathrib (Madinah) to visit relatives, and on the way back to Makkah she died at al-Abwa', between the two cities, and was buried there. Years later the Prophet (s.a.w.a.) stopped at her grave and wept (Ibn Sa'd, al-Tabaqat). Al-Samhudi's Wafa' al-Wafa' places her grave at al-Abwa'; some writers place it in al-Hajun, the cemetery of Makkah.\n\nThis ziyarat is given in the Shia manuals of Hajj, such as Sayyid Muhammad Rida al-Golpayegani's Manasik al-Hajj and Sayyid Jawad Husayni Shahrudi's Adab al-Haramayn, without a narrated source."
